# BENCH PRESS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Bench Press is a bilateral upper-body compound exercise designed to develop horizontal pushing strength through coordinated shoulder and elbow extension.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the foundational exercises for developing upper-body force production, pressing strength and structural robustness.

---

# Philosophy

The Bench Press develops maximal horizontal pushing capacity.

Although striking is not performed while lying on a bench, improvements in upper-body force production can transfer to punching performance when integrated with technical training.

CAS selects the Bench Press when increasing pressing strength supports the athlete's overall physical profile.

